     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Topical antistaphylococcal abx for soft-tissue swelling w/o fluctuance (eg paronychia): triple antibiotic ointment (bacitracin + neomycin + polymyxin B) or mupirocin, + warm compresses or warm H2O/antiseptic (chlorhexidine, povidone-iodine) soaks x10–15 min several times a day"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Blepharitis, severe/refractory (after 1st-line warm compresses + eyelid hygiene): topical abx — erythromycin, bacitracin (PO tetracyclines reserved for severe, refractory cases)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Bact balanitis: clindamycin cream (anaerobe sus); mupirocin cream (strep/staph sus)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": {
      "rule": "auto",
      "value": 1
     },
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "-    Caution: topical antimicrobials (eg bacitracin, neomycin) = common Eti of allergic contact derm"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
